---
title: Two runners sharing one log
---
sequenceDiagram
  participant A as Runner a
  participant L as The log
  participant B as Runner b
  Note over A,B: Claiming a task
  Note over L: A task request lands. Both runners read it.
  A->>L: claims the key
  B->>L: claims the key
  Note over L: The first claim in the log wins: runner a owns the task.
  Note over A,B: Holding it
  A->>L: alive, once a minute
  A->>L: hold: waiting, no run started yet
  A->>L: hold: kept, before the first run
  Note over A: a starts the run once it reads kept back from the log.
  Note over A,B: Runner a is cut off
  Note over A: Its kept tasks go on. Its waiting tasks stay unstarted.
  Note over L: The lease of a ends 30 minutes after its last alive message.
  B->>L: claims a's waiting tasks
  Note over B: b takes them over and runs them. Kept tasks stay with a.
  Note over A,B: Runner a is back
  L->>A: reads the log before any run
  Note over A: a drops each task that moved to runner b.
